# Experiment output. Two different things live here.
#
# results/<alg>/runs/<name>/{train,test} is the archive: one directory per run,
# named for the command that reproduces it, never overwritten. That is tracked --
# every training log and every test session, so a later reader can plot something
# nobody has plotted yet and check it against the run that produced it.
#
# results/<alg>/ outside runs/ is live scratch the controller and the agent pass
# files through. Every run overwrites it, so which run any of it belongs to is
# unknowable: 474 MB and 39k files that are not evidence of anything.
#
# Checkpoints are tracked too. They are 562 MB of tensors that barely compress,
# which is the whole reason to think about it -- but without them the archive
# cannot be tested against, only read, and a run you cannot re-evaluate is not a
# reproducible result. The cost is that re-training and re-committing a
# checkpoint keeps both copies in history forever, so replace them deliberately.
/results/*
!/results/*/
/results/*/*
!/results/*/runs/
!/results/*/runs/**

# Dataset: keep what cannot be rebuilt, drop what can.
#
# Tracked (~8 MB): bw_r.txt and k_paths.json, which define the topology and the
# frozen candidate set every result indexes into and which cannot be regenerated
# (see dataset/README.md), plus the traffic-matrix sources prepare_dataset.py
# needs, so a clone can build the rest.
#
# Ignored: the generated iperf3 script trees (dataset/prepare_dataset.py rebuilds
# them), the full GEANT archive when only 96 matrices are used, and the notebooks.
dataset/*/*
!dataset/*/*.json
!dataset/*/*.txt
!dataset/*/*.md
!dataset/*/traffic_generator/
dataset/*/traffic_generator/*
!dataset/*/traffic_generator/*.pkl
!dataset/*/traffic_generator/*.json
!dataset/*/traffic_generator/*.py
!dataset/*/traffic_generator/*.md
!dataset/*/traffic_generator/traffic-matrices/

# Vendored Enero traffic data. The gym environment reads .demands files from
# here, so a clone cannot train without them -- but the GEANT directories hold
# 2644 matrices where 24 are indexed. Track the topology, the candidate paths and
# the matrices the configs actually name; ignore the rest (~85 MB), which
# dataset/convert_*_to_enero.py rebuilds.
A-Traffic-Engineering-Method-Using-RouteNet-Based-Actor-Critic-Learning-in-SDN-Routing-main/Enero_datasets/**
!A-Traffic-Engineering-Method-Using-RouteNet-Based-Actor-Critic-Learning-in-SDN-Routing-main/Enero_datasets/**/
!**/NEW_32node_144tm/**
!**/NEW_32node_24tm/**
!**/NEW_Geant_s3/EVALUATE/Geant.graph
!**/NEW_Geant_s3/EVALUATE/k_shortest_paths.json

# Live scratch written by the Ryu controller and the delay tracer.
artifacts/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store
